{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Moses returned.</b> The meaning is an expression of returning, for besides the fact that knowledge of Israel's response had already preceded the Creator — for He knows the hidden things in a person's kidneys, and all the more so the revealed things — He further returned the words a second time, and the reason is to praise the response, as I shall explain shortly. Or it may intend, according to the statement of Amram and Zimri, of blessed memory (Mekhilta), that HaShem said to Moses: ״Return to Me their response.״ Therefore it says <b>וַיָּשֶׁב</b> — meaning that because of the response that HaShem told him, ״Return it to Me,״ etc., that is what he did, for otherwise who would report to the One who knows everything, blessed is He." "<b>The words of the people, etc.</b> The intention is not that he reported back that they accepted to act, but rather he reported to HaShem the manner of the order of the response — that they all answered together, in the way I explained. And it was not for informational purposes; rather, the intent in this was to glorify and exalt the nation of Israel regarding several good qualities that the manner of the response would express. And therefore Moses returned the words before HaShem, in the manner of His saying (I Chronicles 17:21): ״וּמִי כְעַמְּךָ יִשְׂרָאֵל גּוֹי אֶחָד״ — ״And who is like Your people Israel, one nation.״"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:30:02.215120855Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}